#N canvas 20 20 3300 2400 12;
#X text 20 20 m_streich -- the Waldorf Streichfett's device layer \, and the only file that talks to it. Told what to play \, as m_volca is \, and polled for presence \, which the Volca cannot be: it answers the identity request. Nothing it sends is decoded \, and nothing goes on param. ref/device/streichfett.md, f 84;
#X text 20 150 creation arg 1: the Pd channel the Streichfett's own channel 1 lands on (33 on the device) \, required. inlet 1: selector-prefixed -- notes <note> <vel> <dur> \, cc <controller> <value> \, program <n> \, note <note> <vel>. outlets: none., f 84;
#X text 20 250 Wired from c_synth \, not sent: no bus carries a sounding note (C-2). Selector-prefixed \, m_volca's four \, so a new capability costs one route argument here and nothing in c_synth or u_root (ref/architecture.md)., f 84;
#X obj 20 460 inlet;
#X obj 20 540 route notes cc program note;
#X obj 20 660 unpack f f f;
#X obj 20 800 makenote;
#X obj 20 1000 noteout;
#X obj 460 660 unpack f f;
#X obj 460 740 t b f;
#X obj 460 830 f;
#X obj 460 1000 ctlout;
#X obj 900 660 + 1;
#X obj 900 1000 pgmout;
#X obj 1300 660 t b;
#X msg 1300 730 fail m_streich bad-selector;
#X obj 1300 800 s err;
#X obj 1780 900 loadbang;
#X obj 1780 950 f \$1;
#X obj 1780 1000 t f f f f;
#X text 1780 1060 The channel goes in cold \, off the right outlets \, before any value can arrive \, and not as a creation argument: Pd does not warn about an extra one (item 63)., f 60;
#X text 20 1080 unpack fires right to left \, so duration and velocity are in makenote before the note triggers it. makenote owns the note-offs \, and it is safe here because the Streichfett has one channel \, set cold at load (ref/device/volca.md \, makenote is safe here)., f 60;
#X text 460 1100 The t b f is load-bearing: ctlout's controller is its cold inlet and unpack sends the value first \, so wired straight through every CC would go to the previous controller., f 56;
#X text 900 1080 + 1 because pgmout is 1-based (item 228): this inlet means the wire number \, 0 for the first sound., f 60;
#X text 1300 870 The reject is a real error: it means c_synth and this file disagree about the interface. C-8, f 66;
#X obj 2300 660 unpack f f;
#X obj 2500 1900 r panic;
#X obj 2500 1960 t b;
#X msg 2500 2020 0;
#X obj 2500 2080 ctlout 123;
#X text 2300 740 note bypasses makenote \, because a held key must not release itself: the off comes from the key \, as velocity 0 from c_synth. Panic covers the droning makenote prevents. It reuses the one noteout., f 62;
#X text 2700 1900 Panic is All Notes Off \, CC 123 \, since the note inlet can leave a note sounding. The value is 0 and the controller the creation argument \, so only the channel has to arrive \, on inlet 2., f 62;
#X obj 20 1700 loadbang;
#X obj 20 1750 del 2000;
#X obj 20 1800 f \$1;
#X obj 20 1850 print m_streich-channel;
#X text 300 1750 Prints the channel it got \, since a wrong count of creation arguments loads in silence. C-9, f 66;
#X obj 1300 1300 c_devid 62;
#X obj 1300 1400 c_presence m_streich 3 120;
#X msg 1300 1480 240 \, 126 \, 127 \, 6 \, 1 \, 247;
#X obj 1300 1700 midiout;
#X obj 1700 1400 loadbang;
#X obj 1700 1450 f \$1;
#X obj 1700 1500 - 1;
#X obj 1700 1550 div 16;
#X obj 1700 1600 + 1;
#X text 1300 1780 c_devid 62 is Waldorf's manufacturer byte \, 0x3E \, which no other device in the rig sends. The 120 ms stagger keeps its reply clear of the Launchpad's and the nano's on the one sysexin (ref/module/presence.md)., f 50;
#X text 1700 1660 The port is derived from the channel block \, (block-1)/16+1 \, as m_nano's is: 33 is port 3., f 40;
#X text 1300 1980 c_presence's second outlet stays unconnected: this file holds nothing that goes stale while the Streichfett is away. c_presence reports a loss and u_present re-wires., f 50;
